Hi Yanjun,

4000! I imagine you could get pretty far just using the offspring at all bi-allelic SNPs trying K=10 and K=20.

How do you identify SNPs anyway? Using GATK or similar on the founders, the offspring, or both? Run time is linear in number of SNPs, so if you can only bother imputing SNPs you'll analyze downstream, you'll save yourself some time on the imputation.

Hope it goes well.

Best,
Robbie

PS Sorry I addressed you as "Zan" above

On Fri, Oct 27, 2017 at 9:43 AM, Zan Yanjun <yanj...@gmail.com> wrote:

> Good suggestions. We have 4000 offsprings, I will trying those again.
